{"case_id":"C040","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry point","API protocol","state","configuration","input semantics"],"confidence":92,"affected_functions":["wuffs_vp8__decoder__set_quirk","wuffs_vp8__decoder__get_quirk","wuffs_vp8__decoder__workbuf_len","wuffs_vp8__decoder__decode_frame","decoder.set_quirk!","decoder.get_quirk","decoder.workbuf_len","decoder.decode_frame?"],"reason":"H0 only instantiates wuffs_webp__decoder and therefore exercises QUIRK_HAS_ALPHA_SIDE_CHANNEL only through WebP's fixed internal transition to value 1 after decode_alph?. It does not fuzz the public VP8 decoder protocol directly: enabling, disabling, querying, or changing the quirk across call-sequence states; supplying independently controlled alpha-prefix bytes; or testing work-buffer lengths around width*height plus the VP8 workspace. Those semantics directly control slice trimming and the final swizzle, making the omitted direct API/configuration surface fuzz-worthy even though valid WebP ALPH inputs cover one integrated path.","evidence":["H0 declares wuffs_webp__decoder dec and passes only wuffs_webp__decoder__upcast_as__wuffs_base__image_decoder(&dec) to fuzz_image_decoder; it never constructs a wuffs_vp8__decoder or calls a quirk API.","S1 adds public QUIRK_HAS_ALPHA_SIDE_CHANNEL and branches for it in decoder.set_quirk! and decoder.get_quirk.","The WebP path invokes this quirk only as this.vp8.set_quirk!(key: vp8.QUIRK_HAS_ALPHA_SIDE_CHANNEL, value: 1), so H0 cannot independently vary its value or transition it back to zero.","When enabled, decoder.decode_frame? computes wh = width * height, rejects work buffers shorter than wh, trims args.workbuf by wh, and uses the prefix as an alpha side channel during the final swizzle.","decoder.workbuf_len adds wh only when quirk_has_alpha_side_channel is true, creating configuration-dependent allocation boundaries not independently varied by H0.","The source contains the explicit comment TODO: trimmed should be args.workbuf immediately before decoder.swizzle!, highlighting sensitive coupling between the prefix-adjusted buffer and output conversion."],"recommended_action":"Add a direct VP8 stateful fuzz target that varies QUIRK_WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT and QUIRK_HAS_ALPHA_SIDE_CHANNEL values and ordering, checks get_quirk, queries workbuf_len, tests exact and boundary-short work buffers, controls alpha-prefix contents independently, and calls decode_frame across valid and invalid call sequences and destination pixel formats."}
